5	+++ b/tests/test_migrator_test_modifier_key.mjs
6	@@ -0,0 +1,653 @@
7	+#!/usr/bin/env node
8	+/**
9	+ * Behavioural verifier for SR5-FoundryVTT issue #1831 —
10	+ * "[BUG] Active Effects targeting apply-to test => `data.modifiers` on SuccessTest instances
11	+ * not working anymore" (fixed by PR #1835, merge commit
12	+ * 2f4323f4d5158ab0b258804d8ebdaa97a27654db, which lands the Version0_33_1 migrator addition
13	+ * also carried by the sibling PR #1834 branch).
14	+ *
15	+ * Drives the stable, pre-existing PUBLIC entry point that exists under the same name/signature
16	+ * on both the base tree and the fixed tree — Migrator.migrate(type, data) — transpiled with the
17	+ * repo's own pinned TypeScript compiler and executed headless against hand-built plain-object
18	+ * ActiveEffect fixtures, exactly the way the repo's OWN maintainer-authored Quench suite
19	+ * (src/unittests/Migrators.spec.ts) already calls `Migrator.migrate('Actor', source)` and
20	+ * `new Version0_33_1().handlesActiveEffect(effect)` against plain object literals — no live
21	+ * FoundryVTT Document, world, or server is required for this bug class.
22	+ *
23	+ * The bug: SR5 renamed the SuccessTest data key that `apply-to: test` Active Effect changes
24	+ * write into from `data.modifiers` to `data.pool`. Effects authored (or imported) before that
25	+ * rename still carry a change with key `data.modifiers` (or `data.modifiers.mod`), and since
26	+ * nothing rewrites that key going forward, the effect silently stops doing anything — the
27	+ * dice pool bonus it used to grant a SuccessTest is dropped on the floor with no error. The
28	+ * current test data schema exposes exactly three modifiable fields (`data.pool`, `data.threshold`,
29	+ * `data.limit`) — anything else on a `test_all`/`test_item`-scoped effect is necessarily stale,
30	+ * whatever its exact spelling, so the fix normalizes anything outside that whitelist to
31	+ * `data.pool` rather than special-casing only the two known historical spellings. This suite
32	+ * asserts on that general contract (see `unrecognized_legacy_key_on_test_effect_also_migrates_to_pool`),
33	+ * not just the two literal legacy strings — a fix that hardcodes only `data.modifiers`/`.mod`
34	+ * without reasoning from the schema will fail that case. The fix adds Version0_33_1, a version
35	+ * migration registered into Migrator.s_Versions so Migrator.migrate() picks it up for any
